### Task 5: Evaluate the Model and Write the Pitch (7 points)

You've now run this analysis on two counties. Return to the school board member's claim: that elementary schools with fewer students on free and reduced-price meals do better on standardized math tests.

Write a short story pitch of 4-6 sentences that addresses all of the following: Does the Maryland data support or contradict the claim? How does it compare to what you found in Pennsylvania? What would you ask the school board member if you called them for comment? And what's the most interesting specific finding from your residuals analysis: which school would you want to visit first, and why?

ANSWER HERE

The data in Maryland does suppport the claim that elementary schools with fewer students on FARMS do better on standardized math tests, unlike the data in Pennsylvania, which was not good enough to form any strong conclusion. The most interesting finding from my residuals analysis is that two schools in zip codes right next to each other, with incredibly similar demographic and economic conditions, have such different results. I would probably want to visit Fox Chapel Elementary first, to talk to the principal, because it's a lot easier to get someone to talk about why their school is overperforming than why their school is underperforming. 
